Z||000000||TRiAD||12-07-2001||06:46 PM||||Hey, I just acquired (by a stroke of luck) my secong freshwater ray...a Potamotrygon hystrix!<P>I traded my Silver arowana for it, and you can see the silver shark catfish and flying fox behind him...<P> <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0QgAwIB8XgPf8oTFYaxn3*e8NqsoJqUylh!CS68SinjTnrgB2PgxMaKnFg2c8BmIzImcQzA3iKYj12qXCPx10kB9rkHQfCq3N4C4Iw0*0UtI/Teacup-hystrix-ray.jpg"> <P>Anyone else keep these?<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0RAAAAN8VWdTblRDE93zkbJ*AbWuOFSwE0rtNS2h23KCe3aGgj1O!JDqud!IoFt1NPvdq6rh9ef*226xJh!nSf*vv2Id5gL8WoDCkDX*tCeM/1985-Signature-2.gif">    <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B> ~ Photoshop rendition of planned modifications</I></FONT>||||reg||6
Z||000001||baptistheart||12-07-2001||06:57 PM||||How big is that ray?<BR> My nephew has a couple small crabs that are pretty cool.<BR> Didn't know you could get things like that all we ever had was your standard goldfish.<P>------------------<BR>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000002||TRiAD||12-07-2001||07:04 PM||||She's maybe 4" diameter, at the most. <BR>According to your source, they'll get anywhere from 9-18" diameter at adult size, in about 3 years. <P>They can be ordered on the net, and larger cities have shops that usually will carry them. In IL, Sailfin in Champaign stocks them, as does Charlie's Aquarium in Pekin (occasionally). I'm sure there are others...<P>||||reg||1
